<title>UK: UK Labour welcomes 2nd Manchester airport runway.</title>
<headline>UK Labour welcomes 2nd Manchester airport runway.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's opposition Labour party on Wednesday welcomed the government's go-ahead for a second runway at Manchester airport, in north west England.</p>
<p>Confirmation of approval for the runway, widely leaked in Wednesday's media, was expected later in a written parliamentary answer.</p>
<p>Labour's environment spokesman, Frank Dobson, said the extra runway would provide a real boost to jobs and economic development in northwest England.</p>
<p>He also welcomed a package of work pledged by the airport to ensure protection of the local environment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
